# App errors

Convex throws structured `ConvexError` payloads through `@pompeii/errors`. The client parses those into `ClientError`. Do not `throw new Error(...)` or `throw new ConvexError("string")` for anything the client should handle.

Codes are domain-scoped, then use-case. Generic codes (`INTERNAL`, `UNAUTHENTICATED`) only when the failure is actually generic. Product failures live under `codes/<domain>/<use-case>.ts` (`AppErrorCode.weddings.createWedding.NAME_REQUIRED`). Messages live in the catalog. Do not pass a message into `throwAppError`. Tests live in `packages/errors/test/`, not `src/`.

```ts
// BAD
throw new Error("Unauthenticated");
throwAppError(AppErrorCode.VALIDATION);

// GOOD
throwAppError(AppErrorCode.UNAUTHENTICATED);
throwAppError(AppErrorCode.weddings.createWedding.NAME_REQUIRED);
```

- Convex: `import { AppErrorCode, throwAppError } from "@pompeii/errors/convex"`
- Client: `clientErrorMessage` / `parseClientError` from `@pompeii/errors/client`
- New client-facing failure: add a use-case file under `packages/errors/src/codes/<domain>/` first
- Impossible states can stay `INTERNAL`
